# Aurum — core rules

Full spec: `docs/MASTER_PROMPT.md`. Working conventions: `CLAUDE.md`. Read both first.

## Mandate (v1, frozen)
- Fusion Markets MT5 Zero **demo only**; XAUUSD symbol discovered at runtime.
- Intraday only; flat before 20:00 London force-flat; no overnight/weekend exposure.
- H1 = regime, M15 = setup/invalidation, M5 = trigger, ticks/M1 = execution realism.
- Completed candles only (a 10:35 decision sees the H1 bar that closed 10:00); as-of joins on close time.
- One position at a time; broker-side stop loss on every trade.
- Costs: $2.25/lot/side commission, real bid/ask spread, configurable slippage.
- Deterministic rules first; ML later as meta-filter only; no DL/RL.

## Non-negotiable safety rules
- Live trading blocked by default (`aurum.core.safety`): non-demo accounts need AURUM_MODE=LIVE + exact AURUM_LIVE_ACK + promotion.yaml sign-off. BACKTEST/SHADOW never send orders.
- Strategies return Signals only; `OrderIntent` requires an approved `RiskDecision` and a `stop_loss`.
- Idempotency key on every order; reconcile on startup and after every action.
- Force-flat must work after disconnect/restart. Kill switch via `KILL` file / `aurum kill`.
- Never use a bar before its close time; buys fill at ask, sells at bid.
- Record every trial in the ledger; never report only the best; never tune on the sealed test; never auto-promote.
- Secrets only in `.env`; never log passwords.
- Never weaken a safety rule to make something work — raise it with the user.

## How to work
- One phase at a time; stop and ask before the next. Phase report in `reports/phase_<n>.md`; ADR per important decision.
- Small conventional commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`), no attribution trailers.
- Tests with the code; `uv run ruff check && uv run mypy && uv run pytest` must be green.
- Type hints everywhere; docstrings state units (price/points/lots/money) and time semantics (open vs close, UTC).
- Aware UTC datetimes only; inject `ClockPort` instead of calling `datetime.now`.
- `MetaTrader5` imported only inside functions in `aurum/adapters/mt5/`.
- Ask when ambiguity affects trading logic, risk or data correctness. Too-good results → suspect a leak.
- Never add a dependency without stating why.
